{
    "consent": {
        "content": "Human Research Ethics Committee (HREC) \u2013 Consent Form\n1.\tI have read the Information Sheet and agree to take part in the research project.\n2.\tI have had the project, so far as it affects me, and the potential risks and burdens fully explained to my satisfaction by the research worker. I have had the opportunity to ask any questions I may have about the project and my participation. My consent is given freely.\n3.\tI understand the purpose of the research project and it has been explained that my involvement may not be of any immediate benefit to me.\n4.\tI agree to participate in the activities outlined in the participant information sheet.\n5.\tI understand my participation is voluntary and that I am free to withdraw my information from the project before the analysis.  \n6.\tI have been informed that the data collected from this project may be published in a journal article, academic theses, conference paper, pre-print archive, Open Science repository, and other forms of publication.  \n7.\tI have been informed that in the published materials I will not be identified and any personal information that could identify me will not be divulged. \n8.\tI consent for the use of my data by the same or other researchers for any future research purposes. I understand any resulting identifiable personal information will be removed or changed before it is either shared with other researchers or made accessible on a public data repository.\n9.\tI understand my information will only be disclosed according to the consent provided, except where disclosure is required by law. \n10.\tI am aware that I should keep a copy of this Consent Form, when completed, and the attached Information Sheet."
    },
    "information": {
        "content": "Dear Participant,\nYou are invited to participate in the research project described below.\nWhat is the project about?\nThis research project seeks to explore how various characteristics of technology impact the way users perceive and interact with these systems. Participants will take part in interactive sessions set in a game-like environment, where adjustments will be made to specific features of the systems being used. By observing these interactions, we aim to gain insights into how these technological attributes influence user perceptions and behaviours. The insights gained from this study could play a significant role in guiding the development and improvement of future technologies, enhancing how they are designed and experienced by users across different contexts.\n",
        "title": "Interactions with Artificial Intelligence"
    },
